<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="037" project="spaarke-ontology-platform-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Signal writer accepts Do-lane subjects: event, To Do, work assignment</title>
    <phase>3 Evaluator, Signal lifecycle and read</phase>
    <gate>007, 008, 024, 039 complete</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Writes secured Dataverse rows for three new subject types; a wrong grouping matter is a data-exposure or worklist-grouping bug that does not error.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Extends task 030's closed derivation set with the same verified pattern; the security judgements were made in FR-14, D-31 and D-33.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>007, 008, 024, 039</deps>
    <tags>bff-api,dataverse,security,signals</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-5 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Extend SignalWriter so sprk_event, sprk_todo and sprk_workassignment subjects derive their grouping CORE record (matter or project) through CoreAncestorResolver (D-34), write the typed regarding lookup and resolver trio, and carry the subject's due date on the Signal, refreshed while the Signal is open.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE backend developer. Ownership and grouping are part of the write, not a follow-up.</role>
  <goal>The writer creates and reconciles Signals for the three Do-lane subject types against real dev rows, with sprk_matter derived and owning business unit from that matter, and sprk_duedate set from the subject.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>D-16 (spec section 9; v4-prototype-vs-solution #12): the writer can group a Signal under a matter only for a matter or a communication subject and refuses event, To Do, work assignment and service request (SignalWriter.cs ~:224-244, ~:485-495). D-16 adds matter derivation via sprk_regardingmatter for the three Do subjects, and says what a task filed under a PROJECT (no matter) does is decided in this task and flagged. D-13: the Do lane re-raises only when the subject's date changed since resolution, so the Signal must carry the date it last saw (sprk_signal.sprk_duedate, task 007). D-27: an event's due date is sprk_duedate. Task 008 granted the writer AppendTo on sprk_event, sprk_todo and sprk_workassignment (D-29).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/SignalWriter.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/unit/domain/Signals/SignalWriterTests.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/integration/seam/Signals/SignalWriterSeamTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Workspace/TodoRegardingBuilder.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner">Scope (D-16, as amended by D-34): accept sprk_event, sprk_todo and sprk_workassignment as subjects; their CORE record comes from CoreAncestorResolver (next constraint), never from a hand-written lookup walk. sprk_servicerequest stays refused. NOTE: CoreAncestorResolver treats sprk_workassignment itself as CORE (a work-assignment subject is its own core record, and its sprk_regardingmatter is NOT an ancestor), so a work-assignment subject hits the open question O-22: see escalation.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner">AMENDED 2026-10-07 (D-34, answers D-16's project-filed question): derive each subject's CORE record with CoreAncestorResolver.ResolveStampsAsync(subjectEntity, subjectId) (origin/master Services/Dataverse/CoreAncestorResolver.cs). CoreTarget or Derived with exactly one matter or project stamp: write it to sprk_matter or sprk_project (task 007), never both. NoAncestor: the D-35 path. Error: refuse (log, meter, write nothing). Do not derive a core record any other way; the closed sprk_regardingmatter derivation from task 030 is replaced by this call for every subject type, including matter and communication.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner">AMENDED 2026-10-07 (D-35, replaces D-31's "To Do owner's BU" wording): an item with NO matter and NO project (NoAncestor) gets a Signal with both core-record columns null, OWNED BY THE TO DO'S OWNER (ownerid = that systemuser, set in the create; the writer holds Assign on sprk_signal), visible to that owner only through task 038, and shown in their Do lane under "Not filed". Read back ownerid. This is the only case with no core record.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner">AMENDED 2026-10-07 (D-33, D-34): call task 039's resolver path with the CORE record (matter or project, if any) AND the subject as parents for every subject type. A Secure answer (a Secure matter or a Secure project) makes the Secure Record Owners team the owner; otherwise owningbusinessunit = the CORE record's business unit. D-33's narrow skip (a To Do with no matter filed under a Secure project) is still applied (O-24). Restricted and Limited are never skipped.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: sprk_signal.sprk_duedate = sprk_event.sprk_duedate (D-27; never sprk_finalduedate), sprk_todo.sprk_duedate, or sprk_workassignment.sprk_responseduedate. Write it on create AND refresh it on reconcile while sprk_signalstatus is Open or Acknowledged; never change it on a Resolved Signal (it is the date the Signal last saw, which D-13's date-change rule compares).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: everything task 030 guarantees still holds for the new subjects: create-first then reconcile, owning business unit from the grouping matter read back and verified, typed regarding lookup plus the ADR-024 trio in one call, lowercase brace-stripped ids, refusals logged at Error with EventId and metered, the dedicated writer identity only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the dedupe key format and the episode are NOT changed here; task 031 changes BuildDedupeKey (D-13). Do not edit BuildDedupeKey in this task.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: if this task changes src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api, state the Placement Justification in the PR citing .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md, and measure publish size against a FRESH build of master from a short path with file counts compared on both sides. Ceiling 60 MB.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: column-name assertions for the three subjects are paired with the live seam test.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: before opening a BFF PR, run /conflict-check.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner">COORDINATION WITH uac-r2 (owner 2026-10-07): (1) Before starting, fetch origin/master and re-read the current uac-r2 implementation this task depends on, and name the files (with commit) in the completion record: SecureChildLineage.cs, config/secure-record-owner-role.json, RecordOwnershipResolver (I-6), RecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter, CallerRecordAccessProbe, tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.Ledger.cs, ADR-034 and its amendments, ExternalCallerContext (ADR-003), CoreAncestorResolver (FR-26 core-ancestor stamps, D-34). (2) Check uac-r2's open PRs and active work for overlap (gh pr list --state open; the uac-r2 current-task.md and TASK-INDEX in C:\code_files\spaarke-wt-unified-access-control-r2 if present) and run /conflict-check. (3) Reuse uac-r2's mechanisms; never build a parallel one. Any change to uac-r2-owned files (the lineage list, the owner-role config, the ledger) goes through uac-r2's review, with the PR linked in this task. (4) If the uac-r2 code has changed in a way that invalidates this plan, STOP and escalate rather than adapting silently.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Signal persistence and ownership</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-024-polymorphic-resolver-pattern.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/030-signal-writer-progress.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/security-roles.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Core-record derivation (uac-r2)" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Dataverse/CoreAncestorResolver.cs">ResolveStampsAsync: CoreTarget / Derived / NoAncestor / Error. The ONLY way this task derives the grouping record (D-34).</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare the rigor level and reason per root CLAUDE.md section 8, then load the knowledge files above before touching code.</step>
    <step order="1">Count, live, the event / To Do / work-assignment rows that have sprk_regardingmatter, only a project, or neither.</step>
    <step order="2">Add the three derivation branches and the due-date mapping; replace the matter derivation with CoreAncestorResolver (D-34); implement the D-35 owner-only path and the D-33 resolver call and narrow skip.</step>
    <step order="3">Refresh sprk_duedate on reconcile for open Signals only.</step>
    <step order="4">Unit tests for each subject, matter and project core records, the D-35 owner-only path, the D-33 secure answer and narrow skip, and the resolved-Signal freeze; seam tests creating and reconciling one Signal per subject type as the writer against spaarkedev1, cleaned up afterwards.</step>
    <step order="5">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task to the completed marker, AND set this POML status element to completed. Both, or scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1 fails the next push.</step>
    <step order="6">Record any deviation from this POML, and the live counts of matter-, project- and not-filed subjects, in projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the writer gets an access-denied creating a Signal for any of the three subjects after task 008, STOP and report the privilege; do not request or add one.</trigger>
    <trigger>CoreAncestorResolver also treats sprk_workassignment and sprk_servicerequest as CORE; D-34 names only matter or project. If an item's core record is a work assignment or service request (spec section 11.1 O-22), STOP and ask the owner; do not fall back to a matter or to Not filed on your own.</trigger>
    <trigger>If CoreAncestorResolver returns more than one core stamp for one item (for example both a matter and a project), which one is THE core record is not decided (O-23): STOP and ask the owner.</trigger>
    <trigger>D-34 gives a To Do filed under a Secure project a core record (the project) and its Decision Record a lineage lookup (sprk_project), which removes the premise of D-33's narrow skip. Whether the skip is retired is not decided (O-24): keep applying it and ask the owner.</trigger>
    <trigger>COORDINATION WITH uac-r2 (owner 2026-10-07): if, on re-reading origin/master, the uac-r2 code this task depends on (record access, ownership, secure children, grants, the route ledger) has changed in a way that invalidates this task's plan, STOP and escalate rather than adapting silently.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test .NET</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/SignalWriter.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/domain/Signals/SignalWriterTests.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/seam/Signals/SignalWriterSeamTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an event and a To Do each filed under matter X, when written, then each Signal has sprk_matter = X (from CoreAncestorResolver), the typed regarding lookup and trio set, and owning business unit = X's business unit, verified by read-back. A work-assignment subject is held until O-22 is answered.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given each subject, when written, then sprk_signal.sprk_duedate equals the subject's sprk_duedate (event, To Do) or sprk_responseduedate (work assignment).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an open Signal whose subject's date changed, when reconciled, then sprk_duedate is refreshed; given a Resolved Signal, when reconciled, then sprk_duedate is unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a task or To Do filed under a project (no matter), when written, then sprk_project is that project, sprk_matter is null, and owningbusinessunit is the project's business unit (D-34).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a To Do with no matter and no project, when written, then both core-record columns are null and ownerid is the To Do's owner, verified by read-back (D-35).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a subject whose core record is a Secure matter or a Secure project, when written, then the Signal is owned by the Secure Record Owners team (D-33, D-34); given a To Do with no matter filed under a Secure project, then the D-33 narrow skip applies (logged, metered) until the owner rules on O-24.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no subject on a Restricted or Limited matter is skipped.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a sprk_servicerequest subject is still refused; BuildDedupeKey is unchanged in the diff.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the writer identity, when the seam test runs for each subject against spaarkedev1, then create and reconcile both succeed and the test rows are removed.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Tests cover the stated contract and edge cases; anything beyond needs a one-line justification in task notes. All tests pass; the BFF builds.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>spec.md FR-14, FR-30 (amended), FR-45(c); D-13, D-16, D-27, D-29.</notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
